ae1abab421347e5f9da2ac2e7cc2092341c6f8cd blob 1008
# Versioned hashing-method resolution

METHOD-QUALIFICATION.md remains accurate for the already executed loader-control
coordinators; their whole-buffer hashing is not retrospectively made compliant.

A new bounded-stream helper now has3 separate SOURCE/DATA checks on the pinned
Node executable: exact data digest, non-regular input refusal, and executable
digest equality. The executable check read112989184bytes in1726 calls with maximum
read65536bytes. No Worker, product or candidate module was launched by these checks.

RUN-SUCCESSOR-V2.mjs.data integrates this helper for the coordinator and child
executable identities. Its only additional differences from the prior source-only
proposal are one helper import and the two executable-hash call sites. All prior
source proposals/records remain unchanged. This is still not an actual execution
packet or permission to retry public80. Hash-helper fault injection/descriptor
retirement is not dynamically proved beyond the recorded normal/refusal cases.

